title: Bread for Munich
subtitle: The peasants have stopped sending milk.
view-if: crisis_bavaria = 1 and bav_bread_done = 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; bav_bread_done = 1
frequency: 100
is-card: true
new-page: true
tags: crisis

= Bread for Munich

Bamberg has blockaded the city, and the priests tell the peasants that the Reds will take their cows and their churches. A hungry city will not fight for long.

- @requisition: Send armed squads into the villages.
- @peasants: Make a deal with the peasants' councils.

@requisition
subtitle: Food for two weeks, and an enemy in every village.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e19_bav_food += 14;
Q.bav_peasants -= 1;
Q.lean_offensive += 1;
Q.crisis_line_2 = 'Food in Munich: ' + Q.e19_bav_food + ' days';
!}

The squads come back with cheese, flour and stories of farmers waiting with shotguns.

@peasants
subtitle: Less food, but it keeps coming, and the countryside stays quiet.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e19_bav_food += 9;
Q.bav_peasants += 1;
Q.lean_unionist += 1;
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 1;
Q.crisis_line_2 = 'Food in Munich: ' + Q.e19_bav_food + ' days';
!}

The Executive promises the peasants that their land is theirs, and pays for milk in Reich marks. Carts start rolling in from the Dachau moor.
